course: dictionary
lesson: 15754
title: The word trio
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trio is a group of three people or things. When you see trio, count: if there are three, it is a trio. «The trio ran to the finish line together.» Three runners, so trio means a group of three.
explain: Trio is also a music word. A piano trio is three players: piano, violin and cello. «The trio played a lovely song at the school concert.» The trio here is a group of three musicians, not three songs.
explain: You can use trio in everyday talk too. «The famous trio of friends went everywhere together.» Harry, Ron and Hermione are a famous trio, because they are three friends who are always together. In maths, a trio is a set of three, so you can sort things into trios.
fact: A trio is a group of three people or things.
fact: In music, a trio is a group of three musicians or singers.
fact: A trio can also be a piece of music written for three players.
fact: A piano trio is piano, violin and cello.
fact: The plural of trio is trios.
fact: Six children can make 2 trios of 3, if each child is in one trio.
exercise: «The trio of friends walked to school together.» How many people are in the trio? | Two | Four | *Three | Five
exercise: «Six children were put into trios for the game.» How many trios can be made, if each child is in one? | *2 trios | 6 trios | 3 trios | 1 trio
exercise: What is a piano trio? | *Piano, violin and cello | A piano and two violins | Three pianos | A piano and a drum
test: «The trio sang a happy song at the school show.» What is a trio in this sentence? | *A group of three singers | A song with no voice | A group of ten dancers | Only one singer
test: What is the plural of trio? | Threes | Trioes | Trio's | *Trios
exam: «Amir, Ben and Chloe form a trio.» How many people are in a trio? | One | Four | Two | *Three
